# ============================================================
# .GITATTRIBUTES — Git LFS tracking
# ============================================================
# The champion model file (crosssell_model_ExtraTrees_v1.joblib,
# ~350 MB) is far over GitHub's 100 MB hard per-file limit. Git LFS
# stores the real file content outside the normal repo history and
# leaves a small pointer file in its place — Render/GitHub/your clone
# all pull the real bytes transparently as long as git-lfs is installed.
#
# Run once, before your first commit:
#   git lfs install
#   git lfs track "*.joblib"
#   git add .gitattributes
#
# If you ever add other large binary files (bigger GIFs, model
# checkpoints, etc.), track them the same way, e.g.:
#   git lfs track "*.gif"
#   git lfs track "*.pt"
# ============================================================
*.joblib filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
